    "english_prompt": "Yes\nTranslate the below sentence into Gujarati .\nIt is imperative that we, as individuals, do not let our cultural heritage disappear into oblivion\ndue to the changing times.\nછે\nઅે જરૂરી કે વ્યિક્તઅાે તરીકે અાપણે અાપણા સાસ્ં કૃિતક મૂલ્યા ે સમય બદલાવાના લીધે ભૂલી ન જઇઅે.\nઅે અિત અાવશ્યક છે કે વ્યિક્તઅાે તરીકે અાપણે અાપણા સાસ્ં કૃિતક વારસાને સમય બદલાવાના લીધે િવસરી ન જઇઅે.\nઅે મહત્ત્વનું કે વ્યિક્તઅાે તરીકે અાપણે અાપણા સાસ્ં કૃિતક વારસાને સમય બદલાતા ગુમાવી દઇઅે.\nઅે અાવશ્યક છે કે અાપણે અાપણા સાસ્ં કૃિતક વારસાને સમય જતા ભૂલી જઇઅે.\nSub-Section Number : 2\nSub-Section Id : 63068045257\nQuestion Shuffling Allowed : Yes\nQuestion Id : 630680730413 Question Type : COMPREHENSION Sub Question Shuffling\nAllowed : Yes Group Comprehension Questions : No Question Pattern Type : NonMatrix\nQuestion Numbers : (82 to 85)\nRead the passage given below and answer the questions\nIn this era of globalization, society seems to be too busy chasing worldly luxuries and often\nneglects healthy lifestyle practices, especially recreational activities. This is because they take\nthe importance of recreational activities lightly. Many people don't realize that recreation\nbrings many benefits to society.\nOne of the benefits of recreation to society is the ability to strengthen relationships, whether\nwith the local community or with one's own family members. This is because through\nrecreational activities, individuals will interact with others around them, thus strengthening\nrelationships. For example, through recreational activities, we can have friendly conversations\nwith neighbors. Furthermore, recreational activities also have the ability to bring peace of mind\nto members of society. This is because through recreation, society can appreciate the beauty\nof their surroundings. For example, through exercises such as jogging, society can breathe in\nand enjoy the refreshing breeze, thus giving peace of mind. Therefore, recreational activities\nare seen as a main foundation for society to relax their minds.\nIn addition, recreational activities are very significant for maintaining physical health. Healthy\nactivities such as jogging, camping, or extreme sports such as skydiving can increase fitness\nlevels and prevent various heart diseases. For example, through activities, especially extreme\nsports that have become the craze among young people, society can increase good\nmetabolism rates for their bodies. Finally, recreational activities can encourage the exchange\nof ideas or thoughts within society. This is because meaningful exchanges can mature society's\nthinking levels. For example, through brief discussions among society, individualistic spirit can\nbe eliminated, and a strong spirit of unity can be established.\nIn conclusion, recreational and recreational activities have many specific benefits that can be\nutilised by each member of society. Therefore, we should prioritise and practice recreational\nactivities in our daily lives because, in fact, a sharp mind lies in a healthy body.\nSub questions",
